"usage: firefly-reports export [-h] [--url URL] [--token TOKEN] [--lang {en,it}] [--debug] [--debug-file PATH] [--trust-insecure-ssl] [--start YYYY-MM-DD] [--end YYYY-MM-DD] [--out DIR] [--layout {yearly,single}] [--scaffold] [--append] [--overwrite] [--map YAML] [--classify-by {category,account}] [--allow-unmapped] [--dry-run] [--validate] [--init] [--no-timestamp] {beancount} Export Firefly III transactions to a plain-text accounting ledger. positional arguments: {beancount} Output format options: -h, --help show this help message and exit --url URL Firefly III base URL --token TOKEN Personal Access Token --lang {en,it} Language of the output --debug Enable debug log to file --debug-file PATH Log file path --trust-insecure-ssl Do not verify TLS certificates at all (self-signed, expired, blocklisted CA); your token can be intercepted. Command line only --start YYYY-MM-DD Start date (YYYY-MM-DD), default: all --end YYYY-MM-DD End date (YYYY-MM-DD), default: all --out DIR Output directory (default: ledger/) --layout {yearly,single} yearly: accounts file + one file per year (default, whole history); single: one file (allows --start/--end) --scaffold First pass: create a draft mapping file from the Firefly accounts (never overwrites; writes no ledger files) --append With --scaffold: add the missing entries to the existing mapping file (keeps its lines, saves a .bak copy) --overwrite With --scaffold: replace the existing mapping file with a new draft (asks for confirmation, keeps a timestamped copy) --map YAML Mapping file (default: ./beancount_map.yaml if present) --classify-by {category,account} Where expense/income accounts come from: the Firefly category (default) or the counterpart account --allow-unmapped Export even without a mapping file or with categories it does not list yet --dry-run Print to stdout, write nothing --validate Run bean-check on the result --init Create main.beancount (and empty manual stubs) next to the output if missing --no-timestamp Omit the generation timestamp (byte-for-byte reproducible output) example: firefly-reports export beancount --scaffold"
